WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.192
PRIYANKA VERGADIA: Are
your existing applications

00:00:02.192 --> 00:00:03.120
holding you back?

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.240
Find out how you can use Anthos
to modernize your existing

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.280
applications and
accelerate performance.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.170
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.730
I am Priyanka, and
welcome to Anthos 101.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.370
In many organizations,
legacy applications

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.500
can hold back
business initiatives.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.720
While new applications
are being developed

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.410
using cloud-native technologies,
most existing applications

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.390
are still large,
monolithic apps that

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.850
run on proprietary
application servers,

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:36.870
incurring high licensing costs,
slow release cycles, and vendor

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:37.710
lock-in.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.830
The lion's share of
existing apps in enterprises

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.190
are written in Java.

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:45.150
And according to a recent
study, 80% of companies

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.430
will continue to leverage
past investments in Java apps.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:51.600
40% of companies will
modify legacy Java apps

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:53.040
for cloud migration.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.010
And 79% will modernize
the Java apps

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.870
with cloud-native technologies
like containers and Kubernetes.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:02.880
Organizations looking to
modernize a Java application

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.319
typically have two
goals in mind--

00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:09.060
one, to adopt modern development
frameworks and architectures,

00:01:09.060 --> 00:01:13.080
and two, move to containers
and adopt DevOps practices.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.500
To achieve these goals,
Anthos offers a solid path

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.780
to modernize your
Java applications

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.780
to realize immediate
operational cost savings,

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.210
reduce dependencies on
higher-cost proprietary

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.840
software, and increase
software delivery speed.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.390
We see enterprise
Java applications fall

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.910
in one of the three
categories, and each

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:37.620
requires that you take a unique
approach to modernization.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.280
First category, applications
using modern frameworks.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:44.170
These are newer apps written
on modern Java frameworks

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.420
like Spring Boot.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.430
The next step for
these applications

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.760
is to take advantage of
Google Cloud-managed services.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.940
Spring Cloud GCP lets
your developers easily

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.950
adopt Google Cloud services.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:58.980
Build tools like Jib and
Cloud Native Buildpacks

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.160
provide an easy way to
containerize these applications

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:06.260
using well-known developer build
tools like Maven and Rattle.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.090
Once containerized, you can
manage these applications

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.479
with Anthos.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.660
The second category is
commercial off-the-shelf

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:14.160
applications.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:15.960
These don't have
the source code.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.990
For these types of
applications, Migrate for Anthos

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.560
allows you to move VMs from
on-premise data centers

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.870
to either VMs running
in Google Cloud

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.290
or to containers running
on Anthos GKE, a cloud

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.540
agnostic implementation
of GKE that

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.940
runs in multiple environments.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.190
This lets you quickly
adopt a modern platform,

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.680
whether on-prem or in the cloud.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.400
And especially useful if
you have a large number

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.850
of applications, as they can be
migrated with minimal effort.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:50.340
Third category, applications
running on proprietary servers.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.220
These are your Java
applications developed

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:56.550
in-house using older
frameworks and often running

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.790
on commercial proprietary
application servers.

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:02.430
Google Cloud provides
a two-step process

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.710
for modernizing
these applications.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.800
First, use Migrate for
Anthos to quickly migrate

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.190
existing applications running
in VMs to containers on Anthos.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.880
You can also migrate off
of commercial app servers

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:18.030
to open-source app servers
to reduce or eliminate

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.540
licensing costs.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.890
Second, refactor and rewrite
migrated applications

00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:26.130
to use modern frameworks like
Spring Boot and Spring Cloud

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:30.630
GCP, and move to a
microservice development model.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.330
Java app modernization
journey with Anthos

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.670
leads to tremendous
cost savings.

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.340
By onboarding the Java
app to containers,

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:42.420
you see a 37% total cost
of ownership savings

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.950
instantaneously.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.700
Then by automating with software
pipeline and refactoring,

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.240
you can see an
additional 78% savings.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.200
There you have it.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.860
With Anthos, you can modernize
your existing Java applications

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.350
and accelerate performance.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.810
Ready to start your
modernization journey?

00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:03.210
Schedule an application
assessment workshop

00:04:03.210 --> 00:04:04.560
with your Google team.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.630
And for more Anthos
content, don't

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:09.730
forget to subscribe and check
out the entire Anthos 101

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:10.230
playlist.

